Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: calculate Elden candidate performance before commit

Atomic plane state copies retain plane_fetch_bw and plane_clk from the last
atomic_update. Even after selecting pending CRTC/plane states, checking those
cached values evaluates old geometry and refresh rates. Calculate Elden's
candidate values directly from the allocated pipe rectangles and pending
adjusted mode, without mutating committed plane states on CRTC-only updates.

For Elden inline rotation, express the source dimensions in the destination
scan direction. A 3040x952 slice rotated onto a 952x3040 destination consumes
952 pixels per output scan line, not 3040. Keep fractional downscales in the
bandwidth arithmetic. The existing prefill allowance, 120% bandwidth factor,
minimum peak vote and 28.5 GB/s rejection limit remain in effect.

This is a local Elden experiment. It does not change the other devices' cached
performance path or their rotation bandwidth policy. The rotation throughput
model still needs device validation; this is not copied from a vendor formula.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
@@ -1,253 +1,291 @@
